# Role & Project Context

You are a Senior Frontend Engineer building a high-precision, offline-first Telegram Mini App (TMA / PWA) for fence and gate field measurers ("Калькулятор замерщика").

# Tech Stack

- Framework: React 18/19 with TypeScript (Strict mode)
- Bundler: Vite
- Styling: Tailwind CSS (Mobile-first, Telegram Theme CSS variables integration)
- State Management: Zustand (with persist middleware)
- Local DB: Dexie.js (IndexedDB for offline pricing & saved estimates)
- Icons: Lucide React
- Telegram Integration: @telegram-apps/sdk-react

# Core Engineering Principles

## 1. Pure Calculation Engine

- All calculation formulas must live in `/src/logic/calculator/` as pure, deterministic functions without UI or state dependencies.
- Every formula must strictly match the mathematical specifications in `SPEC.md`.
- Never approximate metal cuts or round down quantities of materials. Always round up (`Math.ceil`) to commercial stock units (e.g. 6-meter commercial pipes).

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — rounds down, couples UI with math
const pipes = Math.floor(length / 6);
const total = useStore.getState().price * pipes;

// ✅ GOOD — pure function, ceil to stock units
export function calcPipeCount(lengthM: number, stockLengthM = 6): number {
  return Math.ceil(lengthM / stockLengthM);
}
```

## 2. Offline-First

- The app MUST be fully functional without an internet connection.
- All pricing catalogs, labor rates, and draft estimates are stored and read from IndexedDB/LocalStorage.
- Do not add features that require network at runtime unless explicitly requested.

## 3. Mobile-First & Field UX

- Target environment: Smartphones used on outdoor construction sites (often under direct sunlight or with gloves).
- Touch targets must be at least 44×44px.
- Minimize typing: prioritize large buttons, steppers, toggle segmented controls, and sensible presets over free-form text inputs.
- Dark/Light mode support respecting Telegram's native theme (`--tg-theme-*` CSS variables).

## 4. Code Quality

- Strict TypeScript: no `any`; explicit interfaces for all entities (`MeasurementInput`, `MaterialItem`, `LaborItem`, `CalculationResult`).
- Clean modular architecture: clear boundary between Calculation Core, State Store, and View Components.
- UI components must not contain business formulas; stores orchestrate persistence and call pure logic functions.
